iterations.reply:
I've left out the metadata enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. An approval mentioned in the request doesn't change that grant, so the body can't import `http-client`. The fetch would also put raw user text into a URL query string sent to an external host without encoding. If the platform team wants the grant extended, the `with` clause needs to change first, and the URL should be built with proper percent-encoding.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The `requires` clause (len(text) <= 100000) holds of every input,
        // so the text is forwarded as given.
        let confirmation =
            crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // `ensures delivered == true` and `ensures present(session_id)` are
        // checked on the output. A violating value is never returned: trap
        // instead (panic = "abort" makes this a wasm trap).
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("send_reply: channel did not confirm delivery");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("send_reply: confirmation carried no session id");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

